 um to i mean if the  americans are saying that three of their  personnel were injured that doesn't  surprise me because when you go down to  the abbey gate to get in that way there  is a post overlooking the gate  where there's a number of us uh  soldiers stationed i watched them myself  the other day overlooking the crowds and  then just a few meters from them there  is a taliban checkpost and they watch  each other all day and then there's  dozens the other day when we were there  there were hundreds of civilians packed  like sardines banging at the gate hoping  for a chance to get in holding their  papers up to the americans so if there  has been an explosion in that vicinity  there are certainly americans posted  above that wall overlooking everything  and may have been caught up in this we  heard this explosion at 5 40 p.m local  time which is just over an hour ago when  we were there we heard a second  explosion  which was not as strong  and we also heard  sirens coming from inside the airport  and then the taliban had just pushed  everyone back and they had  appeared to have brought in  reinforcements they were  at least double the number of taliban  fighters down there guarding the  entrance as they normally were they were  very tense they were shooting in the air  i saw them break uh a camera from  another journalist  and  they were very tense and and very  concerned and shooting uh frequently  uh charlotte we're also getting more  news from the americans that they  suspect that this was a suicide attack  if that is the case then it does lead  into the direction of isil doesn't it  yeah isil's  mo if you will in kabul is to do  suicide blasts that target civilians  usually they target the shia minority  and they they have been  a constant threat in the back of  everyone's minds in kabul for some years  now although it has been some time since  they have  pulled off any type of  large attack  but they are very much uh  enemies with the taliban and that is o